{
 "name": "Levels built from the curated pool that the uploaded curriculum leaves unused",
 "WHY_THIS_FILE_EXISTS": [
  "tools/vocabulary.py holds 541 words curated for a learner, from the letter-per-level game",
  "that the akshara curriculum replaced. The uploaded curriculum uses none of them, so 320 sat",
  "idle. These 27 levels use 114 of them.",
  "",
  "Same rules as everywhere else: every word starts with the level’s akshara, three words or",
  "more, a wheel of at most 8 tiles, a board inside 5 rows by 7 columns, and no word on a",
  "second board. Every word here also clears the corpus frequency floor, since that is what",
  "vocabulary.py was filtered on.",
  "",
  "Ten of these are aksharas with no level at all before now: গ গা চ চা ছা জ মৌ র রা ল.",
  "The other seventeen are a second level for an akshara that already had one, marked with",
  "·2 - more practice on the same step of the কার series, ordered straight after it."
 ],
 "WHAT_WAS_LEFT_OUT": [
  "জল and মাসি: West Bengal forms. The uploaded curriculum is explicit that a Bangladeshi",
  "   audience gets পানি and খালা, and vocabulary.py predates that rule.",
  "কর: reads as the imperative of করা, which is on the same level.",
  "বর্ষাকাল: means what বর্ষা means, and বর্ষা is on the same level.",
  "Every word in the `describing` theme was set aside before choosing - they are adjectives",
  "   and abstractions, and a level built only of those fails the picture test outright. A few",
  "   are still here where a level needed a third word, each flagged with how to draw it."
 ],
